## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical application of confidential computing across multi-clouds, including key management, attestation, and incident response for privacy-preserving real-time data processing.

## Key Concepts

- Confidential computing TEEs (SGX, Nitro Enclaves, Azure CC)
- Envelope encryption and KMS key management
- Cross-cloud attestation and per-tenant isolation
- mTLS, tamper-evident logging, and incident playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: verify a TEEs attestation before processing sensitive payload
async function verifyAttestation(attestation, expectedAudience) {
  // fetch attestation report from the TEEs
  const report = await fetchAttestationReport(attestation);
  // validate signature, nonce, and audience
  return report.signatureIsValid && report.audience === expectedAudience && !report.revoked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle key rotation across clouds without service downtime?
- What are the trade-offs between SGX vs Nitro Enclaves for latency sensitive workloads?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of practical CORS security fixes, including origin whitelisting, credentials handling, and preflight validation in production applications.

## Key Concepts

- CORS and the ACAO header behavior with wildcards
- Access-Control-Allow-Credentials and the Vary: Origin header
- Preflight OPTIONS request handling
- Authentication boundaries and data exposure risks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express middleware
const ALLOWED_ORIGIN = 'https://app.example.com';

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const origin = req.headers.origin;

  if (origin === ALLOWED_ORIGIN) {
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', ALLOWED_ORIGIN);
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true');
    res.setHeader('Vary', 'Origin');
  }

  if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
    return res.send(204);
  }

  next();
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge security design, token handling, rotation, revocation, and per-tenant RBAC in a globally distributed environment.

## Key Concepts
- Edge computing, token lifetimes, and JWKS
- Per-tenant key rotation and revocation
- Data minimization at edge and canary deployments

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo in-edge validator
function validate(token, jwks){
  const t = decrypt(token);
  const valid = verifySignature(t, jwks);
  return valid && !isRevoked(t.id);
}
```

